.TH ACTION 1 "2026-08-30" "action 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
action \- control one exact effectful connector invocation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B action ls
.br
.B action show
.I name
.br
.B action inspect
.I proposal.json
.br
.B action check
.I proposal.json
.br
.B action run -job
.I job
.RI [ options ]
.I name
.br
.B action run -job
.I job
.RI [ options ]
.B -proposal
.I proposal.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B action
canonicalizes one JSON object, applies an operator-owned deterministic policy,
uses May for exact human review when required, and only then releases the
request to one explicitly named connector from ACTION_PATH.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ls
Print validated connector descriptors as JSONL.
.TP
.BI "show " name
Print one validated connector descriptor.
.TP
.BI "inspect " proposal.json
Validate and print one canonical proposal.
.TP
.BI "check " proposal.json
Validate one proposal without output.
.TP
.B run
Authorize and run one connector. With a connector name, read its input object
from stdin. With -proposal, read both the name and input from the strict file.
.SH RUN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-job " job
Set the stable May job name. Required.
.TP
.BI "-policy " program
Select a deterministic policy. Without it, every action goes to May.
.TP
.BI "-may " program
Select May. The default is ACTION_MAY or may.
.TP
.BI "-record " session
Append sealed action events to an existing Ask session.
.TP
.BI "-ask " program
Select Ask for recording. The default is ACTION_ASK or ask.
.TP
.BI "-timeout " duration
Set the connector deadline. Expiry after request release returns 125.
.SH CONNECTORS
Each executable supports describe and run. Describe prints one descriptor
object. Run reads one complete canonical JSON object before causing an effect
and prints one result object for terminal exits 0, 1, or 75.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACTION_PATH
Colon-separated controller-owned connector directories.
.TP
.B ACTION_POLICY
Default deterministic policy program.
.TP
.B ACTION_MAY
Default May program.
.TP
.B ACTION_ASK
Default Ask program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero is trustworthy success; one is a trustworthy negative result; two is a
broken or invalid pre-release boundary, or a receipted connector report that
no external effect occurred; three is denial; 75 is parked review
or a receipted unfinished connector; 125 means an effect may exist without a
complete trustworthy receipt and must not be retried automatically; 130 is a
pre-release interruption.
.SH SECURITY
Action is not a sandbox. Keep connectors, policy, May, Ask, credentials, and
their state outside model-writable roots. Discovery metadata and executable
digests identify observations, not trust.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ask (1),
.BR context (1),
.BR may (1),
.BR agent (1),
.BR mcp (1)
